# HG changeset patch
# User Betterbird <betterbird@betterbird.eu>
Feature: Linux systray. Also serve an empty com.canonical.dbusmenu on the
  indicator object, so StatusNotifierItem hosts that only implement the legacy
  dbusmenu protocol (notably the GNOME Shell AppIndicator extension) stop
  logging

    Gio.DBusError: ... UnknownMethod: No such interface 'com.canonical.dbusmenu'
    of the object at path /org/ayatana/appindicator/Betterbird_systray_icon

  libayatana-appindicator-glib exports its menu only via org.gtk.Menus, which
  such hosts do not understand.  They learn our object path from the
  StatusNotifierItem "Menu" property and then try to talk dbusmenu to it.
  Answering the (unused) dbusmenu with an always-empty menu keeps them happy
  and costs nothing, since Betterbird intentionally shows no context menu.

